### Generated files
conda/environment.yml
docs/*.md
# ADRs and the design notes they are built from are hand-written records, not
# generated — keep them tracked. ADR-0014 carries its decisions over from
# docs/imperative-fsm-design.md, so that note has to be readable by anyone
# reviewing the ADR.
!docs/adr-*.md
!docs/imperative-fsm-design.md
# So are the per-tool user guides and the passes reference.
!docs/verilower.md
!docs/veriflat.md
!docs/veridump.md
!docs/veriobf.md
!docs/veripp.md
!docs/passes.md
# No PDF is committed. docs/ holds working copies of the IEEE standards and of
# the papers ADR-0014 §C.7 cites; all of them are third-party, redistribution-
# restricted, and the standards are multi-megabyte besides — they have twice
# been swept into a commit by an over-broad `git add`. §C.7 identifies each
# source by full citation and DOI so a reader fetches their own copy.
*.pdf
pkg-build/
conda/build/
